WI-ninoz follow-up, found by probing the merged PR rather than trusting it:
the ratchet PR's per-PR arm was wired into .github/workflows/ci.yml, but the
pipeline that gates merges is Woodpecker — auto-pr polls exactly one
context, ci/woodpecker/pr/woodpecker (woodpecker.yml documents this at the
mypy step, with the 672->682 drift as the receipt for what happens to gates
that live anywhere else). Worse: the live Woodpecker full-suite cron is a
port of the GHA full-suite that DROPPED the check-self-claims step at
cutover, so the gate SECURITY.md names ("gated in CI by
scripts/check-self-claims") has been running NOWHERE live — WI-vanun's gate
existed only in a workflow file no event executes.

Both arms now exist in the Woodpecker pipelines:

- woodpecker.yml `self-claims-gate` (per-PR, in the gating context):
  path-filtered on the claim surface — claims yaml + snapshot,
  self-catalog, overlays, io_primitives + taint catalogues, pyproject
  deps, and the gate scripts. Same install + grammar build as
  full-suite's arm so both analyze the same language set and cannot
  disagree on identical trees.
- full-suite.yml `self-claims-gate` (cron arm): unconditional, so
  analyzer .py changes — which the per-PR filter deliberately skips as
  too heavy — get their verdict drift caught within a cycle.

The GHA ci.yml twin stays as the dormant port, matching the repo's
existing convention for .github/workflows; the woodpecker.yml step
comment names it as non-enforcing.

Also: regenerate docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. The dev push pipeline went RED on
ceaba981 because the doc crossed its 30-commit staleness window (the
tracker-sync commits plus PRs #367/#371 rolled it over). The regen also
picks up the argparse_dispatch linker, which self-categorizes as a
Framework linker via its ADR-3bbb docstring header.

